<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korean Air Lines says 55 survive Guam jet crash.</title>
<headline>Korean Air Lines says 55 survive Guam jet crash.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>At least 55 people survived the crash of a Korean Air Lines (KAL) jumbo jet on the Pacific island of Guam on Wednesday and 27 of them have been admitted to hospitals, an airline executive said.</p>
<p>KAL Vice President Lee Tae-won told reporters that in addition to those in hospitals, a further 28 people were being rescued from the wreckage of the plane. There were 254 people aboard the plane.</p>
</text>
